From e2a89c17275822a31a2a602fd2631684e47996d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rkvenc forward-port <forward-port@local>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 09:42:03 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 42/87] video: rockchip: rkvenc2: sample abort flag before task
 is freed

The forward-port added abort-status propagation to rkvenc2_wait_result():

    ret = rkvenc2_task_default_process(mpp, task);
    if (!ret && test_bit(TASK_STATE_ABORT, &task->state))
            ret = -EIO;

but rkvenc2_task_default_process() calls rkvenc2_task_pop_pending(), which
kref_put()s the task with mpp_free_task. When the blocking waiter returns after
TASK_STATE_DONE the hardware worker has already dropped its reference, so this
put is the last one and frees the task. The following test_bit() then reads
task->state from freed memory, which KASAN reports as a slab-use-after-free in
rkvenc2_wait_result (both statics inline into it). The RK3588 hardware H.264
encoder driven by gnome-remote-desktop hits this on every frame.

The pristine Rockchip BSP returns default_process() directly and never reads
task->state afterwards; the offending read is forward-port-introduced
(23ff47eab6f6). Sample TASK_STATE_ABORT into a local before default_process so
the abort semantics are preserved without touching freed memory. The abort bit
is set before the waiter is released, so the pre-sample sees the same value.

Signed-off-by: rkvenc forward-port <forward-port@local>
---
 drivers/video/rockchip/mpp/mpp_rkvenc2.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/video/rockchip/mpp/mpp_rkvenc2.c b/drivers/video/rockchip/mpp/mpp_rkvenc2.c
index 1bb7ef85a7e71..3549f3bda235d 100644
--- a/drivers/video/rockchip/mpp/mpp_rkvenc2.c
+++ b/drivers/video/rockchip/mpp/mpp_rkvenc2.c
@@ -2715,6 +2715,7 @@ static int rkvenc2_wait_result(struct mpp_session *session,
 	union rkvenc2_slice_len_info slice_info;
 	u32 task_id;
 	bool got_slice;
+	bool aborted;
 	int ret = 0;
 
 	mutex_lock(&session->pending_lock);
@@ -2748,8 +2749,15 @@ static int rkvenc2_wait_result(struct mpp_session *session,
 			}
 		}
 
+		/*
+		 * Sample the abort flag before default_process: it pops the
+		 * task off the pending list and drops the reference that can
+		 * free the task, so reading task->state afterwards is a
+		 * use-after-free once the hardware worker's ref is already gone.
+		 */
+		aborted = test_bit(TASK_STATE_ABORT, &task->state);
 		ret = rkvenc2_task_default_process(mpp, task);
-		if (!ret && test_bit(TASK_STATE_ABORT, &task->state))
+		if (!ret && aborted)
 			ret = -EIO;
 
 		return ret;
